  "modeling_notes": [
    "The current award page is an identity and map index, not a requirement table. Its stated purpose is transfer into a Bachelor of Science in Computer Science, so the separately captured B.S.-destination map is the defensible canonical variant for the one existing Reynolds degree-document identity.",
    "The B.A.-destination map is materially different and is retained below as a complete separate requirement variant. It must become its own degree-variant identity before both variants can be exposed as independently selectable canonical API documents.",
    "Full-time and part-time pages are scheduling variants of the same B.A. or B.S. requirement sets. This composition uses the full-time requirement-bearing sources but removes all semester sequencing and the recommendation to take courses in printed order.",
    "MTH 167 is only recommended when additional preparation is needed and then counts toward elective credit; it is not promoted to an unconditional requirement.",
    "The B.S. page has a one-credit internal conflict: the printed Year Two Fall rows total 17 although the heading says 16, and all printed rows total 64 although the page states 63. All named slots remain visible, while the four destination-directed slots use the 12-credit remainder that closes the official 63-credit total.",
    "UCGS and transfer-elective category gates cite the separate current Approved Transfer Electives source. The program maps' advising substitutions are preserved as exact unsupported constraints instead of being flattened into a universal course list."
  ],
